\fs14\
\f1 \b0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 An NSTableHeaderCell is used by an NSTableHeaderView to draw its column headers. See the NSTableView class specification for more information on how it\'27s used.\
\fs14\
\fs28 Subclasses of NSTableHeaderCell can override \b drawInteriorWithFrame:inView:\b0 , \b drawWithFrame:inView:\b0 , and \b highlight:withFrame:inView:\b0  to change the way headers appear. See the NSCell class specification, and the description below, for information on these methods.\
\fs14\
\fs56\
