¬}\pard \s42 \li1512 \fi-503 \ri1007 \ql \tx1512 drawInteriorWithFrame:inView:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1 \'80(void)\b drawInteriorWithFrame:\b0 (NSRect)\i cellFrame \b \i0 inView:\b0 (NSView\'80*)\i controlView\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Draws the receiver\'27s interior, as described for this same method in the NSCell class specification. NSTableHeaderCell\'27s implementation overrides NSTextFieldCell\'27s to draw the receiver\'27s image if it has one, instead of its string value. If the receiver has no image, it simply draws its string value. This allows column headers to be labeled with images rather than text.\
\fs14\
\fs28 To make an NSTableHeaderCell display an image, use NSCell\'27s \b setImage:\b0  method, which changes the receiver\'27s cell type to NSImageCellType and stores the image provided. To restore it to displaying a text label, supply a new title using \b setStringValue:\b0 , which removes the image and reverts the receiver\'27s cell type to NSTextCellType.\
\fs14\
